      "text": "\n## P2P Architecture (WebRTC)\nHost (Session Creator)\nResponsibilities:\n\nRuns the timer logic locally\nMaintains authoritative state\nBroadcasts state changes to all peers\nActs as signaling coordinator\n\nConnection Process:\n\nHost creates session → Generates peer ID\nCreates WebRTC offer for each joiner\nExchanges ICE candidates for NAT traversal\nEstablishes direct data channel with each peer\nBroadcasts timer state every second + on events\n\nPeers (Joiners)\nResponsibilities:\n\nConnect to host via WebRTC\nReceive state updates\nSend control actions to host\nDisplay synchronized UI\n\nConnection Process:\n\nPeer opens link → Contacts signaling server\nGets host's WebRTC offer\nCreates answer, exchanges ICE candidates\nEstablishes direct connection to host\nSubscribes to state updates\n\nSignaling Server (Minimal)\nPurpose: Only for initial WebRTC handshake\n\nUltra-lightweight REST API or WebSocket\nStores active P2P sessions temporarily (5 min TTL)\nFacilitates peer discovery and SDP exchange\nNo ongoing connection after handshake\n\nWhat it does NOT do:\n\nDoesn't relay timer data\nDoesn't store session state\nDoesn't manage timer logic",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n## P2P Architecture (WebRTC)\nHost (Session Creator)\nResponsibilities:\n\nRuns the timer logic locally\nMaintains authoritative state\nBroadcasts state changes to all peers\nActs as signaling coordinator\n\nConnection Process:\n\nHost creates session → Generates peer ID\nCreates WebRTC offer for each joiner\nExchanges ICE candidates for NAT traversal\nEstablishes direct data channel with each peer\nBroadcasts timer state every second + on events\n\nPeers (Joiners)\nResponsibilities:\n\nConnect to host via WebRTC\nReceive state updates\nSend control actions to host\nDisplay synchronized UI\n\nConnection Process:\n\nPeer opens link → Contacts signaling server\nGets host's WebRTC offer\nCreates answer, exchanges ICE candidates\nEstablishes direct connection to host\nSubscribes to state updates\n\nSignaling Server (Minimal)\nPurpose: Only for initial WebRTC handshake\n\nUltra-lightweight REST API or WebSocket\nStores active P2P sessions temporarily (5 min TTL)\nFacilitates peer discovery and SDP exchange\nNo ongoing connection after handshake\n\nWhat it does NOT do:\n\nDoesn't relay timer data\nDoesn't store session state\nDoesn't manage timer logic",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
